   "text": {
    "L1": "A market is any arrangement where buyers and sellers meet to exchange goods or services for money.",
    "L2": "It can be a haat, a neighbourhood shop, a mandi, a mall, or an online marketplace.",
    "L3": "Goods often travel from a producer to a wholesaler, then a retailer, and finally the consumer.",
    "L4": "Transport, storage, rent and profit add costs at each step, so the final price can be higher.",
    "L5": "Prices depend on supply and demand, not on the shopkeeper alone.",
    "L6": "If supply falls or demand rises, prices tend to rise. If supply is plentiful or demand falls, prices tend to fall.",
    "L7": "For example, floods can reduce tomato supply while demand stays steady, causing prices to jump.",
    "L8": "An informed consumer checks the MRP, asks for a bill, and looks for quality marks."
   },
